  clock: 3  # f255
  nonce: f255  # f255
  message: "Fixed in PR #1714 (dev a18e886229). OPEN QUESTION ANSWERED with an A/B/C on the seven 2026-07-17 deep maps (pretix skipped, 142 MB) at K in {10,100,400}: A = old code, B = test-path symbols out of the population but all edges kept (refuse them only as picks), C = test-path symbols out AND test-sourced edges dropped (the WI-zulij policy). B and C both emit 0 test-path nodes; where they emit fewer nodes than A, the shortfall equals A's test-path count exactly (SwiftyJSON 305-203=102, petclinic 336-145=191, zoxide 231-5=226), so no production node is lost; isolated nodes and components within +-1 either way, containment held in every cell, so the feared seed stranding did not appear. B and C picked the same nodes to within 4% at every budget. Chose C: no new hook, same production_edges order rule the centrality path uses. CODE: format_compact_behavior_map's connectivity branch now runs production_edges(symbols, edges) on the unfiltered list, then drops test-path symbols with the external-boundary placeholders. VERIFIED ON MERGED DEV (same harness, production entry point format_compact_behavior_map(connectivity_aware=True), K=400): test-path nodes express 248/400 -> 0/400, SwiftyJSON 203/305 -> 0/102, spring-petclinic 145/336 -> 0/191, apollo-server 77/400 -> 0/400, caddy 10/400 -> 0/400, zoxide 5/231 -> 0/226, sherpa-csharp 0 -> 0; shipped code equals measured C in 21/21 cells. Production-path tests: test_compact.py::TestConnectivityDefaultPopulation::test_a_test_file_symbol_is_not_a_bridge and ::test_calls_from_tests_do_not_rank_bridge_picks (both red before). Tables: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_10182026_0445.md. NOT measured: the self-analysis map the item cites (9/400) -- a self-run needs owner OK -- and pretix."  # f255
